From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kernel <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: topaz: keep ADSP loader outside simple-bus

The generic simple-bus schema still applies its child-node constraints
to the loader under &soc, even with an explicit qcom,adsp-loader binding
selection. The loader is a software-only platform device with no MMIO
resources; it does not belong on the simple-bus. Place it at the root,
while retaining its phandle to the ADSP PAS. The driver uses that
phandle and is independent of the loader node's location.

Signed-off-by: Kernel <noreply@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
index 046bcf82b..000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
@@ -526,13 +526,11 @@
  * with auto_boot off). The driver is in this series
  * (qcom,adsp-loader); this node is what makes it exist.
  * qcom,adsp-state is the vendor hint for the initial
  * state and matches the live FDT.
- *
- * Sibling of the remoteproc, like the vendor DT: the
- * PAS binding allows no extra children, and the driver
- * resolves the rproc by phandle, so location is moot.
+ * It is software-only, so keep it outside the simple-bus;
+ * the phandle makes its location independent of the PAS.
  */
-&soc {
+/ {
 	adsp_loader: adsp-loader {
 		compatible = "qcom,adsp-loader";
 		qcom,rproc-handle = <&remoteproc_adsp>;
-- 
